From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:49:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: samsung: acpm: defer while the mailbox is missing

The channel loop skips a channel that gets no mailbox, so that one bad
channel doesn't fail the rest. -EPROBE_DEFER isn't such a channel: it
only means the mailbox driver hasn't probed yet. When ACPM probes
first, every channel is skipped, the probe succeeds with "16 channels,
0 usable" and never retries, and everything behind ACPM fails for the
whole boot. On the Pixel 8 Pro the touchscreen then can't enable its
supply ("error -ENODEV: enabling vdd").

This happens when a module load or `udevadm trigger` binds ACPM ahead
of the mailbox, or with fw_devlink=permissive, which drops the
supplier ordering.

Return -EPROBE_DEFER from the probe instead, so it runs again once the
mailbox is there. Keep skipping the channels for any other error, and
the ones whose queues are outside the SRAM. The channels already
requested are freed by the devm action, and the per-channel buffers
are devm allocations.

Fixes: c8e4c99a7852 ("firmware: samsung: acpm: skip channels the AP cannot use")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
---
 drivers/firmware/samsung/exynos-acpm.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/samsung/exynos-acpm.c b/drivers/firmware/samsung/exynos-acpm.c
index 45f3a5616..cbe830b98 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/samsung/exynos-acpm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/samsung/exynos-acpm.c
@@ -738,9 +738,15 @@ static int acpm_channels_init(struct acpm_info *acpm)
 
 		achan->chan = mbox_request_channel(cl, 0);
 		if (IS_ERR(achan->chan)) {
-			dev_warn(dev, "chan %d: no mailbox channel (%pe), skipped\n",
-				 i, achan->chan);
+			ret = PTR_ERR(achan->chan);
 			achan->chan = NULL;
+			/* The mailbox may simply not have probed yet. */
+			if (ret == -EPROBE_DEFER)
+				return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
+						     "chan %d: no mailbox channel yet\n",
+						     i);
+			dev_warn(dev, "chan %d: no mailbox channel (%pe), skipped\n",
+				 i, ERR_PTR(ret));
 			continue;
 		}
 
